The potential vulnerability is related to a Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises from the use of poorly constructed regular expressions that can lead to catastrophic backtracking when processing certain input patterns. If the regex used to validate the email address is overly complex or improperly designed, it may cause the application to hang or crash when presented with specific maliciously crafted email strings, thereby degrading the performance and availability of the service. This issue typically occurs when the regex engine spends excessive time trying to match the input against the pattern, leading to significant delays or resource exhaustion.

